    to approximately RMB 273.8&#160;million (US$38.2&#160;million) for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2025 from approximately RMB 174.1&#160;million
    for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2024. The increase was mainly attributable to combined effects of (i) an increase of gross written
    premiums (&#8220;<span style="font-variant: normal"><b>GWP</b></span>&#8221;) from approximately RMB 1.19&#160;billion for the fiscal
